{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>I have seen:</b> David says: I have seen a tyrant from whom others fear." "<b>And the meaning of מתערה:</b> revealed, acting openly in all evil." "<b>Like a native:</b> it is in construct state and the word 'tree' is missing, and [also] 'flourishing.'" "<b>And the word אזרח:</b> like a native of the land." "<b>And the meaning of אזרח:</b> as though it has many branches, and likewise one who has a large family — and the opposite of this is the stranger, for he is like a severed grain from the tree. And this is the interpretation of the verse: 'I have seen a wicked tyrant, revealed, who is like a native flourishing.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:04.058164410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}